Patch 52. After patch 51.

REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET runs in every generated guest load and store on the platforms with the
physical heap offset (Windows, macOS arm64, Android arm64). It compared the address with
0xE0000000 and selected 0x1000 or 0. It now computes the same value with shifts and an add:
addr >> 29 is 0..7, plus 1 is 8 only from 0xE0000000 up, >> 3 gives 1 or 0, << 12 gives the
offset. The rule itself does not change, and PhysicalHostOffset (rex/system/xmemory.h) keeps the
comparison: it is not in the generated code's hot path, and it is the readable statement of the
rule the generated pch is asserted against.

The generated pch now also asserts the macro against PhysicalHostOffset at 0xDFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF
and 0, next to the existing 0xE0000000. Linux and macOS x86-64 keep offset 0, so their generated
code does not change beyond those asserts.

Test: the new form against the comparison for all 2^32 addresses, once, outside the tree (0
differences); the asserts on every build; CI's PPC tests on Windows and macOS arm64 run the macro.
Measurement: POCO X7, fight.txt, without PGO, as a local edit of the generated header: not yet a
result; the series with PGO decides whether this joins the series.

Upstream: not proposed.

--- a/resources/templates/codegen/pch_h.inja
+++ b/resources/templates/codegen/pch_h.inja
@@ -126,7 +126,8 @@
 
 #if REX_PLATFORM_WIN32 || (REX_PLATFORM_MAC && REX_ARCH_ARM64) || \
     (REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID && REX_ARCH_ARM64)
-#define REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(addr) (((u32)(addr) >= 0xE0000000u) ? 0x1000u : 0u)
+// addr >= 0xE0000000u ? 0x1000u : 0u, without a comparison: the top 3 bits plus 1 reach 8 only there.
+#define REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(addr) ((((((u32)(addr)) >> 29) + 1u) >> 3) << 12)
 #else
 #define REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(addr) 0u
 #endif
@@ -136,6 +137,10 @@
 static_assert(REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0xE0000000u) ==
                   rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0xE0000000u),
               "REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET disagrees with the SDK: regenerate with this SDK's rexglue");
+static_assert(REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0xDFFFFFFFu) == rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0xDFFFFFFFu) &&
+                  REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0xFFFFFFFFu) == rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0xFFFFFFFFu) &&
+                  REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(0u) == rex::memory::detail::PhysicalHostOffset(0u),
+              "REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET disagrees with the SDK at the heap's boundary");
 
 #define REX_RAW_ADDR(x) (base + (u32)(x) + REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET(x))
 
